# The Social Engineering window (SocialWin, see socialwin.c) on the first turn, opened as the F key opens it (social_select, here by
# an open step: the key is the host's own). The faction has only the first model of each category, so the other twelve model places
# are empty frames. The state before the window is first opened (the object as the static initializer leaves it), the note of the
# screen's first visit (with its Tour and Continue buttons), the window as it opens, the mouse over a model button (the box tells what
# it does), over an empty place, over the faction's own box, over each of the effects' buttons (the overview lights the line) and off
# them all; the right button on an empty place of a category panel, on the faction's box and outside them, on the main screen's overview and on an allocation bar (help bubbles, which take a few seconds to come up); the mouse over a model and then the window's own leave handler called by hand (the host sends none); Cancel. The window sits at the
# lower middle of the screen: a place in it is (111 + x, 203 + y) with x and y the object's own.
# The state regions are the window's working numbers (the faction, the models chosen, the effects, the energy numbers), the hover
# markers, the allocation, the rectangles, the three locks, and the game's words the energy and the text variables are kept in.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
